Z||000011||Archie||07-18-2000||10:37 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Will:<BR><B>V8 Archie has an IMSA Fiero for sale at <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com/imsafs.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.v8archie.com/imsafs.htm</A> <P>I am interested in the widebody fenders for front and rear. Does anyone know how much wider than stock these fenders are? IOW, how much wider can I make the wheels/track for front or rear?<P>Also, what are the widest 17" wheels with 3 inch front spacing that will fit on an '88 front suspension?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The IMSA body is 2.5" wider on each side in the front and 3" wider on each side in the rear. (I just went and measured it) You would think that you could then put wheels that were 2.5"F & 3"R wider on the car, BUT YOU CAN'T. Go back and take a real close look at the pictures and compare them to a stock Fiero. Take a look at the rear wheel well openings on my site. You'll notice that the opening is smaller than a stock Fiero. Notice that the body trim piece on the IMSA is one pc. and on a stock Fiero the trim pc. is interrupted by the wheel well. You'll see that the top of the rear wheel opening on the IMSA is 2.5" lower than a stock Fiero. On the front you can compare the relative position of the wheel well opening and the trim pc. and see that it also is 2.5" lower on the IMSA. On my IMSA I have exactly the same wheel & Tire sizes (& brands) as I had on my Chop top car, (the chop top car had stock wheel well openings) When I first bought the IMSA body kit, one of the main reasons I bought it was that I had the impression that I could put wheels that were quite a bit wider than what you could use on a stock Fiero, I was wrong. I didn't notice the smaller wheel wells on the IMSA until after I bought super wide wheels & tires for my IMSA, then I couldn't use them on my car. If you closely look at all the pics. you can find of the IMSA cars, you'll see that none of them have wheels that come out to where they are filling up the wheel wells.<P>I now have the Fino and Finale tooling and kits and those bodies are wider than a stock Fiero and the will allow wider wheels & tires.<P>Hope this helps.<P>Archie||||reg||1
